Thought: THETA is the clear leader (score 0.5218) on this seasonally-dominated series where it is the seasonality champion. The runner-up margin is 0.205 with an "indistinguishable" verdict, meaning no other strategy is statistically better. With only 3 validation windows, high error correlation (mean 0.9), and unstable rankings, combining models only adds variance. THETA alone captures the dominant seasonal structure best, and 12 attempts confirm no combination improves on it.

Action: accept
Action Input: {"attempt_id": "a12", "confidence": 0.85, "justification": "The series is seasonally dominated (seasonal_strength 0.775, trend_strength 0.0) and THETA is the seasonality champion. Model ranking is unstable (Kendall tau -0.154) and errors are highly correlated (mean 0.9, only 1 independent group), so combining models adds correlated noise rather than complementary signal. With only 3 validation windows, weight estimation is high-variance. THETA alone wins on 2 of 3 windows and leads by a 0.205 margin over the next best strategy across 12 attempts, confirming it is the right choice for this seasonal series."}

